# Own-wording spells of Humblewood Campaign Setting and Humblewood Tales (2014 rules). TEXT = {name: [summary, full]}.
TEXT = {
"Ambush Prey": ["Self, 1 hour. You turn invisible and gain Advantage on Stealth checks. Moving 5 ft or more ends it. Your first attack on an unaware target adds 1d6 damage, then the spell ends.",
 "Self, 1 hour. Predatory primal energy hides you completely. You become invisible and have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks to stay hidden. The invisibility lasts for the whole duration, but it ends if you move 5 ft or more from the spot where you cast the spell.\n\nWhile you remain invisible, your first attack against a target that is unaware of you deals an extra 1d6 damage. Making that attack ends the spell.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you cast this spell using a slot of level 3 or higher, the extra damage of that first attack rises by 1d6 for each slot level above 2."],
"Elevated Sight": ["Self, Concentration, 1 minute. Place an invisible sensor up to 120 ft above you and see through it as if flying. You are Blinded while you do.",
 "Self, Concentration, 1 minute. You send your gaze skyward and project your vision into an invisible sensor that appears up to 120 ft above you. Through it you see in every direction at once, as if you were flying. The sensor moves with you and keeps its height relative to you.\n\nAs a Bonus Action you can change the sensor's height, up to a maximum of 120 ft above you. While you look through the sensor you are Blinded. You can switch between the sensor's view and your own eyes at any time during your turn."],
"Feathered Reach": ["Self, 1 minute. Your arms become wings. Fly up to double your Speed as a Bonus Action, leap upward, glide as a Reaction, and jump with Advantage and triple distance.",
 "Self, 1 minute. Your arms change into powerful wings and your fingers into long feathers. When the spell ends the feathers fall away and you drift gently to the ground as your arms return to normal. While it lasts you gain these benefits.\n\n**Flight.** As a Bonus Action you can fly up to double your Speed. You must land when the movement ends. You take no fall damage while the spell is active.\n\n**Propel.** You can launch yourself upward a distance equal to half your Speed. You can do this once per turn and combine it with a normal jump.\n\n**Glide.** When you fall, you can use your Reaction to stiffen your arms and glide on the wind. You can fly up to your Speed in any direction and choose where you land.\n\n**Leaping.** You have Advantage on Strength (Athletics) checks to make a long or high jump. You need no 10 ft run-up and you triple your jump distance.\n\nTo gain these benefits your hands must be free of shields and heavy weapons, and you cannot be encumbered."],
"Globe of Twilight": ["15-ft Sphere around you, Concentration, 10 minutes. Starry shadow hides your chosen allies and dazzles everyone else, who risk Blindness on a failed Wisdom save.",
 "15-ft Sphere centered on you, Concentration, 10 minutes. You fill the area with a sphere of night sky dotted with tiny stars. The twilight hides your allies and plainly lights your enemies. The area is lightly obscured by magical shadow, and small constellations twinkle within it.\n\nOnly light from a spell of level 3 or higher can properly illuminate the area. Nonmagical light does not work inside the sphere, and other magical radiance gives only dim light in a 5 ft space.\n\nWhen you cast the spell, choose any number of creatures you can see. While in the sphere, those creatures are concealed by the shadows. They have Advantage on Dexterity (Stealth) checks and can try to hide at any time. Because the area is lightly obscured, creatures inside have Disadvantage on Wisdom (Perception) checks to see anything outside it.\n\nAll other creatures in the area are dazzled by the stars and have Disadvantage on all Perception checks inside the sphere. When such a creature enters the area for the first time or starts its turn there, it must succeed on a Wisdom save or be Blinded until the end of its turn."],
"Gust Barrier": ["Self, until the end of your next turn. Ranged attacks against you have Disadvantage. Melee attackers who hit you make a Constitution save or are flung 10 ft and knocked Prone.",
 "Self, until the end of your next turn. You spread your arms and let the air around you gather into a protective shell. Until the end of your next turn, any ranged attack against you is made with Disadvantage.\n\nA creature that hits you with a melee attack must make a Constitution save against your spell save DC. On a failure, it is flung up to 10 ft away from you and knocked Prone."],
"Invoke the Amaranthine": ["Self, 10 minutes casting, 24 hours. Roll two d20s and assign each to attack rolls, skill checks, or saving throws. Use them as Reactions to replace creatures' rolls within 60 ft.",
 "Self, casting time 10 minutes, duration 24 hours. You call on an Amaranthine to give you insight into the Great Rhythm that moves all things. When you cast the spell, roll two d20s and write down the results. For each die, choose whether it is for an attack roll, a skill check, or a saving throw. You can choose the same option for both dice.\n\nFor the next 24 hours, you can replace the roll of any ally or enemy you can see within 60 ft with one of your recorded numbers whose type matches that roll (attack roll, skill check, or saving throw). The target still adds its normal modifiers to the number, but otherwise the recorded number counts as the die result.\n\nTo do this you must use your Reaction, present your holy symbol, and speak the name of the Amaranthine whose power you called. You can do it after the roll is made but before the outcome is decided. The spell ends after 24 hours or when both dice have been used."],
"Mend Plants": ["Touch cantrip. Repair a tear in a living plant, sprout seeds and foliage, make a 5-ft cube of plants flourish, or give a plant 1d4 Temporary Hit Points.",
 "Touch. Drawing on primordial magic, you fill nearby plants with vitality. Choose one of these effects.\n\n**Mend.** You instantly repair one break or tear in a living plant you touch, such as torn leaves, a scorched branch, a scar in bark, or two broken pieces. The damage can be no larger than 1 ft in any dimension. The repair leaves no trace.\n\n**Sprout.** You cause a plant without foliage to grow leaves, make a planted seed sprout, or restore the ability to sprout to a dead seed pod.\n\n**Flourish.** You make a 5-ft cube of living plants burst with foliage such as leaves and grass. The growth can be thick enough to hide a Medium or smaller creature, or overgrown enough to be difficult terrain. You choose which when you cast the spell.\n\n**Vigor.** You touch a living plant or plant creature and give it 1d4 Temporary Hit Points."],
"Shape Plants": ["Touch, 1 hour. Reshape plant life in a 5-ft cube. Thorny growth becomes difficult terrain dealing 2d4 Piercing per 5 ft moved. Willing plants may keep the shape.",
 "Touch, 1 hour. You call on gentle natural magic to change how plants grow. Any plant life you can see within range that fits in a 5-ft cube can take whatever shape you like.\n\nIf the plant is a bramble or can grow thorns, you can turn the area into difficult terrain that deals 2d4 Piercing damage for every 5 ft a creature moves through it. You can also raise or lower the number of flowers, vines, leaves, thorns, branches, or fruits on any plant you shape.\n\nAfter 1 hour the magic fades and the plant returns to its normal shape. If you can talk with the plant, by speak with plants or a similar ability, you can try to persuade it to keep its new form. Plants have different attitudes, and one will probably refuse a form that is too far from its natural shape. If it agrees, then at the GM's discretion it keeps the shape you gave it and the change becomes permanent.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you cast this spell using a slot of level 5 or higher, the cube of plant life you can affect grows by 5 ft for each slot level above 4."],
"Spiny Shield": ["Self, Reaction, 1 round. When a melee attack hits you, a force barrier cuts the damage by 2d4 and deals that much Piercing to the attacker. Ranged attacks face a +2 AC cover.",
 "Self, casting time 1 Reaction, 1 round. A barrier of magical force spikes appears between you and an attacker. Until your next turn, when a melee attack hits you, the barrier reduces the damage you take by 2d4 and deals the same amount of Piercing damage to the attacker.\n\nThe barrier does not reduce damage from ranged attacks, but it still gives you a +2 bonus to AC against them for the duration, as if you had cover.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you cast this spell using a slot of level 2 or higher, both the damage reduction and the damage dealt rise by 1d4 for each slot level above 1."],
"Stellar Bodies": ["Two stars orbit you for 1 minute, shedding 10 ft of dim light. Melee attackers within 5 ft risk 1d8 Radiant per star. An action sends a star at a foe for 4d8 Radiant and a Blinding flash.",
 "Self, 1 minute. You create two small stars that orbit you. They twinkle pleasantly and shed dim light in a 10 ft radius centered on you.\n\n**Protection.** If a creature within 5 ft of you hits you with a melee attack, it must make a Wisdom save or take 1d8 Radiant damage for each star orbiting you.\n\n**Streak.** Once per round on your turn, you can use your action to send one star streaking at an enemy. The star is used up in a blinding flash. Make a ranged spell attack against an enemy within 120 ft. On a hit the target takes 4d8 Radiant damage and must make a Constitution save or be Blinded until the start of your next turn.\n\nThe spell ends when its duration runs out, when you fall unconscious, or when you have used all your stars.\n\n**At Higher Levels.** When you cast this spell using a slot of level 6 or higher, you create one extra star for every 2 slot levels above 4. Each extra star orbiting you adds 5 ft to the radius of the dim light."],
"Veil of Dusk": ["60 ft, Bonus Action, Concentration, 10 minutes. A creature is cloaked in shadow and silence, gaining +1 AC and Advantage on Stealth checks.",
 "60 ft, Bonus Action, Concentration, 10 minutes. You speak an incantation toward a creature within range and wrap it in a veil of darkness and silence. For the duration, the target gains a +1 bonus to AC and makes Stealth checks with Advantage."],
}
